From: Scott Iveland <scott.iveland@adtran.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 16:05:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: raise carrier for internal GDM MACs at open

In 6.18 phylink_create() clears the netdev carrier at creation time.
Internal GDM MACs (the embedded switch conduit on GDM1 and the PON
MAC on GDM2) skip phylink at open/stop since the guard restored in
992-97, so nothing raises carrier again: the netdevs stay NO-CARRIER
and all TX through them is dead, taking down the LAN. On 6.12 these
netdevs had no phylink object at all, so they kept the register-time
carrier-on default and worked.

Raise carrier manually when opening an internal port and drop it on
stop, restoring the effective 6.12 behavior. External-PHY ports are
unaffected.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2219,6 +2219,11 @@ static int airoha_dev_open(struct net_de
 		}
 
 		phylink_start(dev->phylink);
+	} else {
+		/* phylink_create() clears carrier and internal GDM MACs
+		 * never start phylink, so raise carrier manually
+		 */
+		netif_carrier_on(netdev);
 	}
 
 	netif_tx_start_all_queues(netdev);
@@ -2283,6 +2288,8 @@ static int airoha_dev_stop(struct net_de
 	if (airoha_is_phy_external(port)) {
 		phylink_stop(dev->phylink);
 		phylink_disconnect_phy(dev->phylink);
+	} else {
+		netif_carrier_off(netdev);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
